{
  "title": "Wait for failed batch spectators before finalizing logs",
  "description": "When a pilot exits nonzero in wait_for_all_games, the code \
calls spectator_proc.terminate(), kills remaining pilots, records result -1, \
and immediately removes the session from the active set. The orchestrator can \
then call finalize_game while the spectator is still running and flushing game \
event files. This creates a race where merge_game_log, error aggregation, and \
website export can read partial files. Terminate the spectator process tree, \
wait with a bounded timeout, force-kill if necessary, and only mark the \
session ready for finalization after process exit. Reuse one shutdown helper \
for normal and failed paths where practical. Add a test proving finalization \
cannot begin until the spectator has exited and a process-level test covering \
final log writes after termination.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 1,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "orchestration",
    "concurrency",
    "logging",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-07-11T11:32:21.127-07:00",
